 "problem": "When scanning transactions for silent payment eligibility, verifying whether a P2SH input is P2SH-P2WPKH evaluates the scriptSig before checking for a witness. Non-segwit P2SH inputs can carry scriptSigs up to 10,000 bytes, causing unnecessary script evaluation overhead during block or transaction scanning.",
 "card": "Skips scriptSig evaluation for non-segwit P2SH inputs during BIP352 silent payment input parsing. Under BIP352, only P2SH-P2WPKH inputs are eligible, which require a witness, whereas consensus mandates an empty witness for legacy P2SH spends. By checking the witness stack and public key size before executing script evaluation, the scanner avoids parsing scriptSigs of up to 10,000 bytes on legacy P2SH transactions. A bug here could cause silent payment wallets to miss eligible inputs and fail to detect incoming funds.",
